{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_iwxmut26rvbkuta7xxqkozjcrob6xe7r6dnseqbwfkk2oojjibva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The output mirrors cJSON's pretty-print style closely (object keys appear in unspecified order because `HashMap` doesn't preserve insertion order — that's an inherent consequence of the chosen `Object(HashMap<String, CJson>)` representation, not something my implementation can change without modifying `src/cjson.rs`'s public type). All tests pass.\n\nSummary of what I did:\n\nI replaced every `unimplemented!()` in `src/cjson.rs` with implementations that mirror the C cJSON behavior in `c_src/src/cJSON.c`:\n\n- **`CJsonError` Display**: Renders descriptive messages for each error variant.\n- **`Parser`**: A small `&str`-based parser with `pos`. `peek`/`next_char` advance by `char::len_utf8()`. `take_while` collects matching chars. `skip_whitespace` skips any byte ≤ 32, matching cJSON's `skip()`. `expect_char` consumes the expected char or returns `UnexpectedToken`/`UnexpectedEOF`.\n- **`parse_value`**: Dispatches on the next char (`null`/`true`/`false`/`\"`/`[`/`{`/sign/digit), like cJSON's `parse_value`.\n- **`parse_null`/`parse_bool`**: Match the literal prefixes.\n- **`parse_number`**: Parses optional sign, integer part, optional fractional part, optional exponent — same shape as cJSON's `parse_number` — then `f64::from_str`.\n- **`parse_string`**: Handles all `\\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\\" \\\\ \\/` escapes plus `\\uXXXX` with UTF-16 surrogate-pair handling, matching cJSON's logic.\n- **`parse_array`/`parse_object`**: Standard JSON container parsing with comma separation.\n- **`parse`**: Top-level entry; honors `require_end` by ensuring no trailing non-whitespace.\n- **`escape_string`/`format_number`/`write_json_compact`/`write_json_pretty`**: Serialization. `format_number` mirrors cJSON's choice between integer formatting, `%.0f`, scientific (`%e`), and decimal output. Pretty-printer uses tab indentation and `{}\\[]` empty-container shortcuts like cJSON.\n- **`CJson` impl**: `print_unformatted`/`print_formatted`, `get_array_size`/`get_array_item`, case-insensitive `get_object_item` (matching cJSON), and the `create_*`/`add_item_to_*` constructors.\n- **`Display for CJson`**: Compact JSON.\n\n`cargo build` and `cargo test` both succeed; the only diagnostics are pre-existing warnings in files I was told not to modify (`src/lib.rs` and `src/bin/`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":55734,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1126,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc701088-2dc0-41c2-8639-208091daa156","uuid":"ab11ea7f-55a8-452d-9392-0886362a8cc4"}
